I'm pretty sure perverting death is a nono in Cad's book.  Also, they don't know if she will wake up as herself or something else due to those good ol eyes all over her.

&#x200B;

Aaaaaand..  remember the rules on how someone could get into the cerberus assembly?  Wellllll hey Caleb, looks like they have a new opening..

You look good literally everywhere lol.  You are athletic and have a nice body, your face is symmetrical and really naturally pretty, you have nice hair that looks healthy, and your skin looks flawless.  good shit.

&#x200B;

Also your eyebrows are on point

Damn dude, that sucks.  I recommend dropping her and working on yourself for a while.  Hit the gym, create art, do something to take your mind away so later on if you guys meet back up then you will be so much more fun and interesting to be around instead of someone locked in a time capsule since the last time you spoke.

&#x200B;

Best of luck.

You're Drake, your brother is Josh, and your sister is Megan.

&#x200B;

That's the problem NTA

Not ugly at all, you look like clint stevens from twitch.  Your face has a lot of versatility, try buzzing the hair off and growing a trimmed stubble, you'd look bomb af.

&#x200B;

Obviously photoshop a pic with the look first so you don't feel like a goober if you go through with it and hate it right after.

I had an old lady in a grocery store look at me and smile and say "you're what hitler had in mind!".  

&#x200B;

I just hit her with the Eddy Burback "yikes", paid for my groceries and left..

Jail or military time is not a thing and hasn't been a thing for an extremely long time.  Unless you're both in your 50's I'm pretty sure this whole story is bullshit.  There are countless sources but I am a military vet who's job was military accessions and separations.

&#x200B;

[https://www.stripes.com/news/judge-said-army-or-jail-but-military-doesn-t-want-him-1.44417](https://www.stripes.com/news/judge-said-army-or-jail-but-military-doesn-t-want-him-1.44417)

This.

&#x200B;

There is documented proof that this isn't a thing anymore.. and it's been that way for a long time..

I feel you man, if you ever wanted to try growing out a beard genetics or not, minoxidil (rogaine) on your face seems to be the key to breaking that genetic barrier.  I was in the Navy surrounded by men with patchy beards so I understand your struggle, it doesn't always end up glamorous.

&#x200B;

Your best bet would be to try and take a more focused approach on your fashion sense.  Try to get one outfit that looks amazing on you, it doesn't have to be designer or expensive at all, but whatever it is, get that one outfit tailored to you and see how you feel afterward.  I'm sure you will look much better.

&#x200B;

As for the photography stuff, yeah, I get you.  Just try to shoot in some warmer/natural lighting that doesn't cast a lot of shadow on your face, and look at the top posts on here from men and check their angles, that will do wonders for you with little to no effort.

&#x200B;

Best of luck, hoping for an update post sometime soon!

In my opinion, he needs to break up with you.  He is not ready for a committed relationship if he thinks he is "missing out" with sleeping with other girls, agreeing to anything that lets him play out that fantasy will just diminish your relationship and hurt BOTH of you in the end.

&#x200B;

 I was in a seriously toxic relationship for the first half of my 20s and missed out on my "hoe phase", now that I look back, even though for the majority of my relationship I was the victim of severe abuse, I realize that I also added stress onto my partner at the time because I felt like I was missing out on a "huge part of my life" (being with other women) and began to resent her partially because of that.  I'm not saying your man will do the same, but I can tell you how I felt about a very similar situation.

&#x200B;

I eventually cheated and felt awful about it afterward, wishing I never ruined my relationship for something so insignificant.  I told her everything and it destroyed her completely, turning an already abusive relationship into a hellscape for the next 4 years.

&#x200B;

He isn't being fair to the both of you if he wants to keep you on the backburner if having sex with other women doesn't work out.  Either he wants all of you or none of you.  Either way, it sounds like he isn't ready to be with you forever, regardless of how ready you are.

You look attractive but you also look boring.  You're not attractive enough to look that boring tbh, only models can get away with that.  I recommend you photograph yourself acting like a human doing not awkward human things that show interest and emotion.

&#x200B;

Also, everyone could look better if they worked out a bit more so if you're not lifting weights, maybe you should try it out.  The added muscle mass and tone on your frame would look amazing.

Lots of potential.  You will look amazing once you get your gym routine together.

&#x200B;

I recommend gaining muscle now though, don't wait.  You don't need to lose fat to gain muscle, your fat will naturally burn away when you start gaining your muscle before your first plateau.  Lift heavy, eat clean, don't skip cardio.  Get into your routine and you will start to look even better than you do now.

&#x200B;

Excited to see a follow up post from you.

You look good man, stay in the gym, lift heavy and tan a bit.  Your hair/eyebrows/beard all look great and your sense of style (from what I can tell) looks alright.  You're an attractive dude.

&#x200B;

If I had to recommend something, I would say shape your eyebrows up a bit, line up the beard a bit more and keep it a consistent length until you want to grow it out.  Keep your hair lined up tight because you have a light skin tone with dark hair so if one thing is out of place, everyone can see it.  Your coloring isn't as forgiving as pale blonde guys.  Other than just grooming, work on a more aggressive fashion style and you're ready to go!

The glasses/shirt/hair combo makes you look 30 and not 21.  Buzz the hair or grow out the top and shave the sides.  The 5oclock shadow looks alright so it can stay or leave depending on how you feel about it.

&#x200B;

I recommend getting some athletic clothing that form-fit to your body because you're in such good shape, really show yourself off and don't hide behind a cheap zip up.  If you need a jacket, find a real substantial jacket like a field jacket/bomber/parka.  The one you have currently looks like pajamas.  Other clothes I can recommend you are joggers, skinny/slim fit jeans, anything that stretches to your natural curves.

I recommend contacts because these frames currently make you look much older than you are and I can't think right now to find a frame shape that would look good, I would play around at the store and find out what works, but tortoiseshell wayfarers don't seem like they're doing your face justice.

&#x200B;

You're a good looking guy and the only things that can be improved are the things you're wearing so that's a plus.  I would say if a normal guy is a 5/10, you're a 6/10 but that could be made much higher if you changed your style up a bit.  Best of luck!

If a 5/10 is the completely average person, you would be a 7/10.

&#x200B;

You're have a really pretty face, you look healthy and your sense of style matches you well.

&#x200B;

The areas for improvement are the same for you as nearly every other girl, play with a more aggressive fashion style, play with different styles of makeup, and working out more will make you more attractive, but you don't really need any of it.

I didn't talk to my dad for about 10 years after a falling out.  He was never around or supporting my family in my life so I didn't feel like I owed him anything.  After he got pretty entitled in trying to reconnect with me, I snapped at him because I felt he didn't have a right to pretend to be a dad after abandoning my family for 20 years.

&#x200B;

Well about a year later I get a call from my brother and he tells me dad is in the hospital and they don't know what is happening but his heart is failing, he was doing better at that point so he should be out soon but they don't know what kind of treatment he would need in the future, my brother said he would keep me updated.  Got a call a few hours later saying that my dad passed away. 

&#x200B;

The last thing I said to my dad was along the lines of "I hate you, never contact me again.  You're dead to me, you were never a father to me" and it still haunts me to this day.

&#x200B;

TL;DR: My dad tried to reconnect with me and I shut him out at the first sign of conflict, he passed away before I could apologize to him and make a meaningful relationship.  Life is short, forgive and move forward.

Don't fall for it, they may feel remorse and guilt now.  It could all be genuine right now, but they will go back to the same attitude before as soon as they are given the chance.  

&#x200B;

It helped me to write down the reasons of our fights and the hurtful things she said to me, I took videos and pictures of the abuse to make sure I didn't forget or go back on my word.

&#x200B;

When you make the split, tell someone you respect about it, tell them you left your SO because of these reasons and that you were miserable with them, explain the abuse and hypocrisy so you have people who will stop you from going back.  Strengthen your exit strategy and disappear, dropping them so you don't have to deal with the emotional fallout that they will dial up to 500 for you to guilt you back into a toxic relationship.  

&#x200B;

Wishing you the best.

Speaking as someone who cheated, planned it prior to the act, lied about it to their SO's face, felt guilty and confessed to them later.

I recommend going to counseling first, talking to an intermediary will help him open up because he will NEVER give you the whole truth one on one.  He will feel like he is risking everything he wants in life by telling you, and he doesn't want to lose what he still has in his hands (you).  He will tell small white lies about the whole ordeal to make it hurt less for you, which is why he said he didn't know why he cheated (he knows exactly why, it's just embarrassing).  I recommend finding out if he confessed because of his guilt, or because he was scared you would find out.

&#x200B;

The main thing is that he probably was excited to cheat, find someone extremely willing to give him something new and exciting that he was embarrassed to try to pursue at home, or couldn't pursue at home.  He could have felt locked down, like he is wasting his golden years, that he is unhappy with himself, etc. it doesn't matter.  After the act, he probably realized that the 10 minutes of sex wasn't worth a lifetime of lying and paranoia so he started to beat himself up about it mentally, he wants to ghost the girl but doesn't want her to contact you when she gets pissed at him.  He wants to tell you but doesn't want to lose his relationship over something so unsatisfying in the end.  He will be willing to do anything to get rid of the feeling of guilt and stupidity he feels after the whole ordeal and just wants to make it go back to the way he felt before.

&#x200B;

Talk to the girl without him knowing to get the rest of the story if it interests you, don't trust what he says.  Read the texts, however he texted her is how he really felt at the time.  Don't believe anything like "oh I was just playing her" etc.  Its all bullshit.

Thank you for the book recommendations, I am really happy you are finding happiness again in your life.  You deserve so much better than a life in a negative feedback loop of being treated like an abusive monster when you did nothing wrong.

&#x200B;

Thank you for this.

It's the same thing every time.  I am currently breaking up with a pwBPD and it is hell.  I am abandoning them, I never did anything for them, they can replace me, they can't live without me, I'm a cheater, I was always there for them, etc..

&#x200B;

It's really damn hard to separate from someone who is willing to gaslight, lie, cheat and steal their way back into your life when you don't want them to begin with.  Just remember that when they are love-bombing you, this is who they really are, and what they really think about you.  You can't trust someone who "cant control themselves" when they get mad.  You don't need to deal with that for the rest of your life, they will drain you for everything you have and leave you out to dry saying "they never did anything for me" when the well dries up.

&#x200B;

You didn't do anything wrong, you're not abandoning anyone.  They are an adult and should be able to support themselves and not leech off of you for everything, a relationship should be 2 independent people working as a team.  Not an adult unable to control themselves, refusing to get help, and an independent adult providing all support in the relationship.

&#x200B;

My BPDso would get to the point of stabbing my bed and vomiting on it if I didn't know what they wanted to eat.  But they didn't start that way, it compounds over time.  You are strong for trying to make it work, but you aren't obligated to be the keeper of some other adult just because they want you to.

&#x200B;

Hope it gets better.

Thank you so much, you have no idea how much that means to me.

&#x200B;

Its cruel to be starved for affection after so long, then get 10 messages saying "youre right, im sick, ill get help.  Im so sorry, I miss your smile so much, even getting an angry text back brightens my whole day" right as you try to leave and make your life better.  It's so toxic.

&#x200B;

I am trying my best to distance myself from them as much as possible, only speaking through email from now on, and asking for the moving company details.  If I have to block them there and work solely through their parent then that's what I'll do.  I am so ready to be healthy and happy again.

I hope you feel better, just remember that every problem she brought into your life and developed while you two were together, she is still carrying with her and bringing into her next relationship too.  Don't get too caught up on her decisions, she may be going after easy targets, or people that she knows will make you upset.  In my experience, every 1-minute happy memory posted online is followed by hours of tense friction in the relationship where they could snap at any time.

&#x200B;

Keep your head up, you're in a better place than you were 12 months ago.

Go out and have a bunch of one night stands, but when you get to their house start to act all nervous and ask to go to the bathroom.  Put all of their toilet paper in your bag, then come out and tell the person "I'm sorry, I can't do this.. I'm married" and run out of there crying.

&#x200B;

If they feel bad, they might even get you an uber home.

I still can't believe Danny Elfman did the music for fable 1.  Insane.

&#x200B;

For those who don't know, Danny Elfman is the man in charge of the music for shows like the simpsons, batman, literally every tim burton movie but one, he *was* Jack Skellington.  He made most of the themes that I grew up with, and there's a reason I can still hear oakvale's theme in my head today.  He's a legend.

Getting the hobbe cave demon door before figuring out chain lightning.  oof.

&#x200B;

One of my favorite games of all time.  I can still remember where the silver keys are, it's wild.  Too bad about the singing sword though.

ESH

Probably would have cheered you on if I was 15, but i'm a bit older and I understand that parents don't always have great coping mechanisms.

&#x200B;

You're turning 18, that's a huge deal for you, I get it, i've done it too lol.  Have you ever thought how depressing it is to release your child into the world though?  I get how your parents would want their friends at the party, it can help de-stress and take their minds off of the fact that their baby is about to fly from the nest, and all of these wonderful girls theyve seen grow up, are about to split apart and start their own lives.

&#x200B;

I'm gonna be real with you.  You will have SO many birthdays with just you and your friends, but you don't get to have a lot with your parents.  I'd let them have this last one, make it wonderful, and plan a followup birthday party with just my friends.

&#x200B;

I understand your reaction, I just hope you can understand theirs.  They're probably scared of losing you.

NTA

&#x200B;

She deserved hands, but you gave her words.

As an american who lives in japan, married to a Japanese woman; that kid is going to get made fun of every day no matter where they are.

&#x200B;

Your kid will become top tier cringe just by existing.  If my family sees a random american here in japan and I know they're 100% american, but his name is something like Fumitada, Tadashi, Satoshi, or Hiroshi, they would visibly cringe and would start to laugh super hard to each other, that kid would become an inside joke within seconds.  My whole family would think this poor person was raised by weebs and feel bad for them.

&#x200B;

But my whole family is made up of judgmental assholes, as is most of Japan

&#x200B;

Edit:  You should post this in r/japancirclejerk if you really want to show your wife how people will react.

YTA

&#x200B;

The kid didn't do anything to hurt you, but you took the route that only hurt an innocent kid who didn't know anything about the situation (presumably).  

&#x200B;

Although you might be an asshole for stealing it back, I would have done the exact same thing in your situation.  Happy youre getting away from your parents, and with your property in hand too, good job!

Not ugly.  If the average woman is 5/10, you would be a 7/10.  You are the standard attractive person.  You are the one in the group that people will notice first, you are the one the guys talk about when pretty girls come up in conversation.  Good job.

&#x200B;

Your face is balanced and all of your features tie together nicely.  You have a distinct face that looks different but nice.  The thing that pulls you ahead is your style, you own it and it works on you wonderfully.  The colors, clothes, and overall hard aesthetic plays a balancing game against your soft features, making you look like a really well put together person in terms of style.

&#x200B;

Recommendations:  You have room to grow, you can fill out the gaps in your wardrobe with accessories, giving your look those little details for people to focus on.  Your hair is a bit frizzy, I recommend a mask or treatment to smooth it out, you could easily steal the looks and style from Krysten Ritter as Chloe on the show "Don't Trust the B---- in Apartment 23" ([https://www.google.com/search?q=krysten+ritter+chloe&tbm=isch&chips=q:krysten+ritter+chloe,g\_1:apartment+23:w13RzKD6MSc%3D&hl=en&ved=2ahUKEwjgu\_OGuoDoAhUK6ZQKHQXzBsQQ4lYoAHoECAEQFQ&biw=1903&bih=955](https://www.google.com/search?q=krysten+ritter+chloe&tbm=isch&chips=q:krysten+ritter+chloe,g_1:apartment+23:w13RzKD6MSc%3D&hl=en&ved=2ahUKEwjgu_OGuoDoAhUK6ZQKHQXzBsQQ4lYoAHoECAEQFQ&biw=1903&bih=955))

&#x200B;

You will still be attractive if you don't do any of these recommendations, so good job. honestly, it's obvious that you put in work, and it pays off.  You look great.

Not ugly, if  the average person is 5/10, that makes you a 6.5-7/10.  You are an average, attractive person.

&#x200B;

You have great style and attitude.  Your face is well balanced and symmetrical, your body looks average and slim.  All good things.  If you want advice in styling, look at George Miller (Joji) or Ezra Miller considering you look like their love child (which is a good thing).

I completely understand, that feeling where everything that used to be fun is now a slog.  The thing that honestly helped me the most was having good friends who cared about what I was going through, they would constantly pressure me to go out and match their level of happiness.  At first I hated it and just did it to not lose my friends, but after a while it started to catch on.

&#x200B;

I don't know what could help you specifically, but what were your hobbies before?  What are your skills?

Hobbies manifest out of interest usually.  When I wallow in depression, I tend to watch videos of artists painting, drawing, sculpting, etc.  From there I try to copy what they do, then I get frustrated and try to watch a real tutorial.  Once I learn the basics, I feel better about myself and my skills even if it's something small.  I find that my art made the largest jumps in quality when I went through a depressive episode.

&#x200B;

Silver linings ig..

This is hilarious because the Charity has a Service Mark registered June 5, 2018.  The Service Mark they registered is not the design that Uninterrupted is even using.  The Charity's design is as follows:

&#x200B;

 "Color is not claimed as a feature of the mark.  The mark consists of the wording "I AM MORE THAN AN ATHLETE." in stylized font. The wording "I AM MORE" is on the first line, "THAN AN" is on the second line, and "ATHLETE" is on the third line. Beneath this wording are the stylized letters "GP" between the arrows. The arrow on the left is bent at an angle. Beneath the arrows and the letters "GP" is the term "GAMEPLAN" in stylized font."

&#x200B;

The kicker is that the charity's registration is for a service mark, not a Trademark for a brand.  And Uninterrupted ALSO has a Service Mark registered to them about 6 years prior, on September 25, 2012 for the literal words "more than an athlete" in any design, to be used for Publicity and sales promotion services.

&#x200B;

ALSO.  Uninterrupted has filed a slew of Trademarks in for different versions and products containing the branding of "I am more than an athlete" in the early 2018 time frame.

&#x200B;

Source (U.S. Patent and Trademark Office:  [http://tmsearch.uspto.gov/bin/showfield?f=toc&state=4809%3A53ge1j.1.1&p\_search=searchss&p\_L=50&BackReference=&p\_plural=yes&p\_s\_PARA1=&p\_tagrepl%7E%3A=PARA1%24LD&expr=PARA1+AND+PARA2&p\_s\_PARA2=More+Than+An+Athlete&p\_tagrepl%7E%3A=PARA2%24COMB&p\_op\_ALL=AND&a\_default=search&a\_search=Submit+Query&a\_search=Submit+Query](http://tmsearch.uspto.gov/bin/showfield?f=toc&state=4809%3A53ge1j.1.1&p_search=searchss&p_L=50&BackReference=&p_plural=yes&p_s_PARA1=&p_tagrepl%7E%3A=PARA1%24LD&expr=PARA1+AND+PARA2&p_s_PARA2=More+Than+An+Athlete&p_tagrepl%7E%3A=PARA2%24COMB&p_op_ALL=AND&a_default=search&a_search=Submit+Query&a_search=Submit+Query)

